From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: The Playport authors <dev@playport.dev>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 10:00:10 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] kk: MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=soft_fp64 lowers 64-bit floats to
 integer code

Apple GPUs have no FP64 and Metal has no double (MSL specification 2.1),
so KosmicKrisp reports no shaderFloat64, vkd3d-proton reports no
DoublePrecisionFloatShaderOps and refuses any shader that declares FP64
(d3d12_device_validate_shader_meta), and DXVK refuses a DXBC double
instruction. DIRT 5's GDK build stops on one such compute shader: its
pipeline fails with E_INVALIDARG.

With the flag, every 64-bit float operation becomes inlined calls into
Mesa's soft-fp64 library (src/compiler/glsl/float64.glsl, Berkeley
SoftFloat), as ANV's fp64_workaround_enabled does on GPUs without FP64
hardware; Mesa enables that for DIRT 5 and DOOM Eternal. Results are IEEE
binary64 with round-to-nearest-even and subnormals; NaN propagation is
relaxed and there is no fused fma.

- The library is built to SPIR-V with the driver (glslangValidator, now
  required for KosmicKrisp; ANV's meson rule) and to NIR at the first
  shader that needs it, kept on the physical device.
- kk_preprocess_nir lowers after msl_preprocess_nir, where functions are
  inlined and ALU ops scalar, which nir_lower_doubles needs. flrp and
  ffma are split first; what is left is 64-bit integer code, which the
  MSL backend writes as long and ulong.
- The device reports shaderFloat64, shaderDenormPreserveFloat64 and
  denormBehaviorIndependence ALL, which vkd3d-proton needs before it
  reports FP64; the fp16 and fp32 denorm modes still cannot be asked for.

It changes only shaders that use a 64-bit float, which could not be
built without it, so it is not in the pipeline cache UUID. It must be
named (MESA_KK_EXPERIMENTAL=all alone does not turn it on).

Linear: PLA-815
Class: feature
Evidence: docs/evidence/2026-11-03-dirt5-xbox-minidump-apiset.md
Offered-upstream: no
---
